   plot="'The Open Boat' follows four men — the correspondent, the captain, the oiler and the cook — in a ten-foot dinghy off the Florida coast after their ship has sunk; they row for thirty hours toward a shore they can see but cannot reach, and the oiler, the strongest of them, drowns in the surf within sight of land.",
