   plot="The poems present brief, enigmatic scenes — a man climbing a mountain and finding a bitter fruit, a creature eating its own heart, a god who admits he is a lie — in which the biblical and the ironic are set against one another, and the reader is left to find the meaning.",
   ctx="1895: the American free-verse experiments of the 1890s, the collapse of the Puritan certainties, and the vogue for the epigram after Whitman and Emily Dickinson.",
