   plot="Martin Eden, a rough sailor, educates himself to win the hand of Ruth Morse, a bourgeois girl; he reads Spencer and Swinburne, writes stories that nobody will buy, is rejected by Ruth's family, and then becomes famous overnight, after which he discovers that success means nothing and that the woman he loved cannot understand him.",
   ctx="1909: the American magazine market, the socialist movement of the 1900s, the intellectual self-education of the autodidact, and the American cult of success.",
