   plot="A manuscript of the 1930s, annotated by a scholar of a later socialist era, records the rise of the Iron Heel, the American oligarchy that destroys the socialist movement after 1912, the failed Chicago Commune and the extermination of the revolutionaries, and the long dark age that follows before the final triumph of the brotherhood of man.",
   ctx="1908: the American labour wars of the 1900s, the socialist movement of Eugene Debs, the Russian revolution of 1905, and the fear of monopoly capital.",
